<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Itō Hirobumi</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1841–1909</span> · Also known as Ito Hirobumi</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Itō Hirobumi (1841–1909) was a Japanese statesman from the Chōshū domain and the first prime minister of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/japan">Japan</a>, serving four times between 1885 and 1901. He led the drafting of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/meiji-constitution">Meiji Constitution</a> of 1889 and founded the Rikken Seiyūkai party in 1900. As the first Resident-General of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/korea">Korea</a> from 1905 he oversaw the Japanese <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/protectorate">protectorate</a>, and he was assassinated at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/harbin">Harbin</a> in 1909 by the Korean nationalist An Jung-geun.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/ito-hirobumi.jpg" alt="Itō Hirobumi" width="320" height="435" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown authorUnknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:IT%C5%8C_Hirobumi.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
